    "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Vectors Whose Angle Is a Non-Special Angle",
    "problem": "The vector $u$ has magnitude $1$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $11,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${27}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to the nearest integer where appropriate.",
    "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =1\\cdot 11\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{27}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =11\\cdot (0.453\\,99…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(4.993\\,89…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈5n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
